.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt MULLVAD-RELAYS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mullvad-relays
.Nd download, select and describe Mullvad VPN relays
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl adorR
.Op Fl C Ar city
.Op Fl c Ar country
.Op Fl p Ar provider
.Op Fl s Ar gbps
.Op Fl t Ar type
.Op Fl L | Fl i | Fl f Ar fields | Fl w
.Op Ar host ...
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lists the relays of the Mullvad VPN, the servers a tunnel can end at,
from the public list Mullvad publishes.
It selects them by place, type, provider, ownership, DAITA and speed,
and prints them as a table, as every field they carry, as chosen
fields for a script, as a count per place, or as the
.Ql [Peer]
section of a WireGuard configuration.
.Pp
The list is downloaded once a day and kept in a cache
.Pq Sx FILES .
A download that fails, or that is not a relay list, leaves the cache in
place, and
.Nm
goes on with the list it has, after saying so on stderr.
.Pp
A relay is selected when it passes every option given, and, when hosts
are named, when its hostname starts with one of them:
.Ar se-got
selects every relay in Gothenburg,
.Ar se-got-wg-001
that relay alone.
Only active relays are selected, unless
.Fl a .
The list arguments of
.Fl c , C , p
and
.Fl t
are comma-separated, and are matched without regard to the case of
ASCII letters.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-f fields"
.It Fl a
Include relays that are not active.
They are flagged
.Ql inactive
in the table.
.It Fl C Ar city
Relays in these cities, each named by its code
.Pq Ql got
or its name
.Pq Ql Gothenburg .
.It Fl c Ar country
Relays in these countries, each named by its code
.Pq Ql se
or its name
.Pq Ql Sweden .
.It Fl d
Only relays that offer DAITA, Mullvad's defence against traffic
analysis.
.It Fl f Ar fields
Print the fields named, comma-separated, as one tab-separated line per
relay, with no header.
The field names are those
.Fl i
shows; a field a relay lacks
.Pq a bridge has no Ql pubkey
is empty.
A name no relay carries is a usage error.
.It Fl h
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl i
Print every field of each relay, one
.Ql name: value
line each, with a blank line between relays.
A field holding a list, such as
.Ql status_messages ,
is printed on one line.
.It Fl L
List the countries and cities of the relays selected, with how many
relays each has, in the order of the list.
.It Fl o
Only relays Mullvad owns, rather than rents from a hosting provider.
.It Fl p Ar provider
Relays hosted by these providers.
.It Fl R
Keep one relay, drawn at random from those selected, each as likely as
the others.
.It Fl r
Download the list now, however old the cache is.
.It Fl s Ar gbps
Relays whose port speed is at least this many Gbit/s, a whole number.
.It Fl t Ar type
Relays of these types:
.Ql wireguard
.Pq or Ql wg
and
.Ql bridge
.Pq or Ql br ,
the relays that carry a tunnel through a censoring network.
.It Fl w
Print the WireGuard
.Ql [Peer]
section for the relay selected: its public key, every address routed
through it, and its IPv4 address on port 51820 as the endpoint, after
a comment naming it.
Only WireGuard relays are considered, and the selection must come down
to one relay: name it, or add
.Fl R .
.El
.Pp
.Fl L , i , f
and
.Fl w
exclude one another, and
.Fl R
cannot go with
.Fl L .
Without any of them,
.Nm
prints a table of the relays selected, one per line, with a header:
hostname, country, city, provider, port speed in Gbit/s, and flags
among
.Ql owned ,
.Ql daita ,
.Ql inactive
and
.Ql notice ,
the last when Mullvad has posted a status message about the relay
.Pq Fl i No shows it .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width MULLVAD_RELAYS_CACHE
.It Ev MULLVAD_RELAYS_CACHE
The cache file, instead of the one under
.Ev XDG_CACHE_HOME .
.It Ev XDG_CACHE_HOME
The directory of the default cache, instead of
.Pa ~/.cache .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.cache/mullvad-relays.json
The relay list as last downloaded, from
.Lk https://api.mullvad.net/www/relays/all/ .
It is downloaded again once it is a day old.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
A relay was selected and printed.
.It 1
No relay was selected; with
.Fl w ,
more than one was; or the list could neither be downloaded nor be
found in the cache.
.It 2
A usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
The relays in Gothenburg and Malm\(:o that offer DAITA:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ mullvad-relays -d -C got,mma
.Ed
.Pp
The countries Mullvad owns relays in:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ mullvad-relays -o -L
.Ed
.Pp
The address and key of every Swiss WireGuard relay, for a script:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ mullvad-relays -t wg -c ch -f hostname,ipv4_addr_in,pubkey
.Ed
.Pp
A WireGuard configuration for a Swedish relay drawn at random, from an
.Ql [Interface]
section of one's own: the private key, and the address Mullvad
assigned when its public key was registered:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cat interface.conf > wg-mullvad.conf
$ mullvad-relays -w -R -c se >> wg-mullvad.conf
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr curl 1 ,
.Xr fetch 1 ,
.Xr wg 8 ,
.Xr wg-quick 8
.Sh CAVEATS
The list is the one Mullvad's web site reads; it is public but not
documented, so a change to its fields comes unannounced.
.Pp
Case is ignored for ASCII letters only:
.Fl C Ar malm\(:o
finds Malm\(:o, and
.Fl C Ar MALM\(:O
does not.
.Pp
Without
.Xr curl 1 ,
the list is downloaded with
.Xr fetch 1 ,
which
.Fx
has in its base system.
